cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "For the code and synthetic benchmark data, cite the version-specific Zenodo DOI after the corresponding release is published. The project concept DOI identifies the archive across versions. The companion manuscript has no separate DOI in the supplied materials."
title: "Green Catalyst Screening: Supporting Data and Code for an Interpretable Chemoinformatics Benchmark"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gagan Sai Amith
    family-names: Pennada
    affiliation: VIT-AP University, India
version: "0.3.0-pre-release"
url: "https://github.com/amith2427/Green-Catalyst-Screening"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23383768"
    description: "Zenodo project concept DOI; this is not a v0.3.0 version DOI."
license: MIT
abstract: "Supporting code and a synthetic chemoinformatics benchmark for auditing regression models, cross-validation strategies, sensitivity to non-causal decoy descriptors, TreeSHAP attributions, and an illustrative Green Performance Index. All reaction data and targets are synthetic; they are not experimental chemistry evidence or validated predictions of catalyst performance. The archived metrics are traceable and consistency-checked, but a complete independent clean rerun has not yet succeeded."
keywords:
  - chemoinformatics
  - synthetic benchmark
  - machine learning
  - model interpretability
  - catalytic alcohol oxidation
  - cross-validation
  - decoy sensitivity
  - TreeSHAP
  - reproducibility
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "An Interpretable Chemoinformatics Benchmark for Evaluating Machine Learning Frameworks, Decoy Sensitivity, and Green Catalyst Prioritization"
  authors:
